  "discovered": "2026-10-16 � the roocamer.gnjoy.game job-intro SPA renders its imagery from the Joymaker CDN (file.joymaker.com). Each job file name comes from the official data endpoint (https://rooc-official-am-api.joymaker.com/api/rooc/job-intro: img_male/img_female per job) and the CDN URL (vite content hash) was extracted from the site bundle asset map (main-BVKl7piB.js). Hashed URLs change on site redeploys � the fetcher records 404s as designed-missing (D-16: graceful, never fatal), and the committed files under public/assets/classes/ keep the panel self-hosted (D-15).",
  "naming": {
    "portrait_female": "class-f-<slug>.png",
    "portrait_male": "class-m-<slug>.png",
    "icon": "class-icon-<slug>.png",
    "slug": "lowercase class name, spaces -> hyphens"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Portrait art exists for every transcendent job on the site EXCEPT Rebellion (the Gunslinger line p8 is completely omitted from the bundle � owner-confirmed). The Rebellion research samples that once lived in assets/ were removed by the owner (2026-10-17): Rebellion portraits are now the DESIGNED-missing state — the committed copies under public/assets/classes/ stay intact, and a fetcher re-run reports them MISSING without failing (D-16).",
    "The site only provides SEVEN base-role icons (p1..p7) � there is no per-transcendent-class icon, so classes sharing a base line share the same icon (e.g. High Wizard and Professor both use the Mage icon). That is the site reality, not a mapping error.",
    "Bard is the male-only job of the Archer second line (site art p5_*_big_22): class-m-bard uses the male art; class-f-bard never occurs in-game (expected_missing). Gypsy is its female-only counterpart: class-f-gypsy uses the female art; class-m-gypsy never occurs in-game (expected_missing)."
